you can try this (untested)
JavaScript:
Game_Player.prototype.updateDashing = function() {
        if (this.isMoving()) {
            return;
        }
        if (this.canMove() && !this.isInVehicle() && !$gameMap.isDashDisabled()) {
            if (Input.isLongPressed("shift")) {
                this._dashing = $gameSwitches.setValue(5, true);
            }
        } else {
            this._dashing = $gameSwitches.setValue(5, false);
        }
    };
so if you use longpress shift (this is around .5 seconds up to 1 second when the switch
flips true.
once the player is moving, it will return, once you stop or move into the wall,
the switch is false (which makes, dashing is false).
change the switch id (5) to your desired switch ID.
you can drop in the code in a new JS and into your folder.

